mparison; po_number/amount stay exact-match since those are unambiguous."}, {"id": "role_string_gap_rationale", "label": "platform_admin/dept_admin vs seeded-realm role-string gap (recurring, now 5+ admin routers)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PROGRESS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No seeded dev-realm Keycloak user holds the exact platform_admin/dept_admin role string rbac.py's ROLE_PERMISSIONS expects. Worked around identically across Collections/Models/global-read-only/Agent-admin/api_keys_admin: the enforcement path is proven live via directly-seeded rows, only the issuance endpoint itself goes untested live. First logged Sprint 3, still open, now blocks a fifth+ admin router."}, {"id": "env_file_makefile_bug", "label": "Makefile COMPOSE missing --env-file .env (Sprint-1-era latent bug)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PROGRESS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "docker compose -f infra/compose/docker-compose.dev.yml did not reliably auto-discover .env from the invoking working directory. Every prior .env-sourced var happened to have a working fallback or be optional, so this was silently broken since Sprint 1 until n8n's Fleet API key (no safe default) needed it. Fixed by always passing --env-file .env explicitly in the Makefile's COMPOSE variable."}], "edges": [{"source": "api_keys_admin_router", "target": "api_keys_module", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/PROGRESS.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "service_auth_module", "target": "api_keys_module", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/PROGRESS.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "service_router", "target": "service_auth_module", "relation": 